cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss EDNA-1, please cite both the software and the Open Research Europe article (DOI to be added upon publication)."
title: "EDNA-1: Behavioral Biometric Human Sensoric Engine for AI"
abstract: >-
  EDNA-1 (Enhanced Detection & Neural Analysis) is a client-side
  behavioral-biometric sensoric engine for AI recognition systems. It senses
  16 channels of human behavior entirely on the user's device and turns them
  into an AI-readable signal vector and Human Confidence Score, so an AI can
  understand the human behind the session — presence, attention, hesitation,
  engagement — and adapt its behavior accordingly. No raw biometric data
  leaves the device; exports carry only non-personalized, salted cryptographic
  hash patterns.
